  "id": "post-hoc-comparison",
  "term": "post hoc comparison",
  "definition": "A post hoc comparison is a comparison among group means that is chosen after the data have been examined rather than planned in advance. It is a type of unplanned comparison, and it uses different statistical tests than planned comparisons.",
